{"bendscript":"0.1","blocks":[{"id":"blk-59199","kind":"heading","level":1,"spans":[{"id":"spn-88499","text":"delegatic"}]},{"id":"blk-59200","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-88500","text":"OS-006 Governance Shim — authorization kernel for the [&] Protocol ecosystem."}]},{"id":"blk-59201","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-88501","text":"Issues signed, expiring "},{"id":"spn-88502","marks":["code"],"text":"AuthorizationBlock"},{"id":"spn-88503","text":"s to destructive edges in OS-011 "},{"id":"spn-88504","marks":["code"],"text":"&body.*"},{"id":"spn-88505","text":" replay flows. Policy-based, deny-by-default, pluggable policy store."}]},{"id":"blk-59202","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-88506","text":"Status"}]},{"id":"blk-59203","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-59205","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-88507","marks":["bold"],"text":"Library:"},{"id":"spn-88508","text":" v0.1.0 production-ready"}]}],"id":"blk-59204","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-59207","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-88509","marks":["bold"],"text":"Tests:"},{"id":"spn-88510","text":" 42/42 (25 unit + 3 integration + 14 MCP tool tests) + 2 body-os end-to-end integration tests"}]}],"id":"blk-59206","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-59209","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-88511","marks":["bold"],"text":"Storage:"},{"id":"spn-88512","text":" in-memory ETS-backed "},{"id":"spn-88513","marks":["code"],"text":"PolicyStore"},{"id":"spn-88514","text":" — Postgres-backed adapter is a future additive release"}]}],"id":"blk-59208","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-59211","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-88515","marks":["bold"],"text":"MCP server:"},{"id":"spn-88516","text":" shipped — 6 tools on the "},{"id":"spn-88517","marks":["code"],"text":"delegatic"},{"id":"spn-88518","text":" namespace (put/get/list/delete policy + authorize + verify) with Anubis stdio/HTTP transport"}]}],"id":"blk-59210","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-59213","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-88519","marks":["bold"],"text":"Deployment:"},{"id":"spn-88520","text":" "},{"id":"spn-88521","marks":["code"],"text":"fly.toml"},{"id":"spn-88522","text":" + "},{"id":"spn-88523","marks":["code"],"text":"Dockerfile"},{"id":"spn-88524","text":" ready for Fly.io ("},{"id":"spn-88525","marks":["code"],"text":"delegatic-mcp"},{"id":"spn-88526","text":", port 4400)"}]}],"id":"blk-59212","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":false},{"id":"blk-59214","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-88527","text":"MCP surface"}]},{"id":"blk-59215","kind":"code","language":"text","text":"delegatic_put_policy       — register or replace a Policy\ndelegatic_get_policy       — look up a Policy by id\ndelegatic_list_policies    — list every registered Policy\ndelegatic_delete_policy    — remove a Policy\ndelegatic_authorize        — issue a fresh AuthorizationBlock\ndelegatic_verify           — verify a block's HMAC signature + TTL"},{"id":"blk-59216","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-88528","text":"Remote agents (body-browser-mcp, body-os-mcp, FleetPrompt's InstallEngine, Graphonomous replay flows) call "},{"id":"spn-88529","marks":["code"],"text":"delegatic_authorize"},{"id":"spn-88530","text":" to obtain the fresh blocks they need for destructive edges per OS-011 §4.4."}]},{"id":"blk-59217","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-88531","text":"This is the "},{"id":"spn-88532","marks":["italic"],"text":"authorization kernel"},{"id":"spn-88533","text":" — the minimum needed to close the OS-011 destructive-edge loop. The full Delegatic spec ("},{"id":"spn-88534","marks":["code"],"text":"delegatic.com/docs/spec/"},{"id":"spn-88535","text":") layers on org trees, memberships, effective-policy computation, and a LiveView dashboard; those are future work."}]},{"id":"blk-59218","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-88536","text":"Contract"}]},{"id":"blk-59219","kind":"code","language":"elixir","text":"# 1. Register a policy\n:ok =\n  Delegatic.put_policy(\n    Delegatic.Policy.new(%{\n      policy_id: \"delegatic://ws-42/ops\",\n      allow_actions: [\"file_write\", \"shell_exec\"],\n      deny_actions: [\"file_delete\"],\n      agents: [\"ops-agent\"],\n      max_ttl_seconds: 300\n    })\n  )\n\n# 2. Directly request authorization for one action\n{:ok, block} =\n  Delegatic.authorize(\n    action_type: \"file_write\",\n    policy_id: \"delegatic://ws-42/ops\",\n    agent_id: \"ops-agent\",\n    approved_by: \"supervisor@acme\"\n  )\n\n# 3. Or build a function ready for the OS-011 Replay `:authorizer` slot\nauthorizer =\n  Delegatic.authorizer_for(\n    policy_id: \"delegatic://ws-42/ops\",\n    approved_by: \"supervisor@acme\",\n    agent_id: \"ops-agent\"\n  )\n\n# 4. Wire it into body-os replay\nBodyOs.Replay.execute(session, trace, authorizer: authorizer)"},{"id":"blk-59220","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-88537","text":"AuthorizationBlock"}]},{"id":"blk-59221","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-88538","text":"Every issued block carries:"}]},{"head":[{"id":"blk-59223","spans":[{"id":"spn-88539","text":"Field"}]},{"id":"blk-59224","spans":[{"id":"spn-88540","text":"Example"}]}],"id":"blk-59222","kind":"table","rows":[[{"id":"blk-59225","spans":[{"id":"spn-88541","marks":["code"],"text":"policy_id"}]},{"id":"blk-59226","spans":[{"id":"spn-88542","marks":["code"],"text":"\"delegatic://ws-42/ops\""}]}],[{"id":"blk-59227","spans":[{"id":"spn-88543","marks":["code"],"text":"approved_by"}]},{"id":"blk-59228","spans":[{"id":"spn-88544","marks":["code"],"text":"\"supervisor@acme\""}]}],[{"id":"blk-59229","spans":[{"id":"spn-88545","marks":["code"],"text":"approved_at"}]},{"id":"blk-59230","spans":[{"id":"spn-88546","text":"ISO8601 UTC"}]}],[{"id":"blk-59231","spans":[{"id":"spn-88547","marks":["code"],"text":"expires_at"}]},{"id":"blk-59232","spans":[{"id":"spn-88548","text":"ISO8601 UTC (capped at "},{"id":"spn-88549","marks":["code"],"text":"policy.max_ttl_seconds"},{"id":"spn-88550","text":")"}]}],[{"id":"blk-59233","spans":[{"id":"spn-88551","marks":["code"],"text":"authorization_token"}]},{"id":"blk-59234","spans":[{"id":"spn-88552","marks":["code"],"text":"\"sha256:<64-hex>\""},{"id":"spn-88553","text":" — HMAC over the other fields"}]}]]},{"id":"blk-59235","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-88554","text":"The token is "},{"id":"spn-88555","marks":["italic"],"text":"tamper-evident"},{"id":"spn-88556","text":", not secret — any consumer can call "},{"id":"spn-88557","marks":["code"],"text":"Delegatic.AuthorizationBlock.verify/1"},{"id":"spn-88558","text":" to detect forgery or expiration."}]},{"id":"blk-59236","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-88559","text":"The HMAC key lives in "},{"id":"spn-88560","marks":["code"],"text":"config :delegatic, :hmac_key"},{"id":"spn-88561","text":". A per-process random fallback is used when unset (fine for tests, unsafe for prod)."}]},{"id":"blk-59237","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-88562","text":"Policy semantics"}]},{"id":"blk-59238","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-59240","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-88563","marks":["bold"],"text":"`action in deny_actions`"},{"id":"spn-88564","text":" → "},{"id":"spn-88565","marks":["code"],"text":"{:error, :denied_by_policy}"}]}],"id":"blk-59239","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-59242","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-88566","marks":["bold"],"text":"`agents` set and `agent_id` not in it"},{"id":"spn-88567","text":" → "},{"id":"spn-88568","marks":["code"],"text":"{:error, :agent_not_allowed}"}]}],"id":"blk-59241","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-59244","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-88569","marks":["bold"],"text":"`action not in allow_actions`"},{"id":"spn-88570","text":" → "},{"id":"spn-88571","marks":["code"],"text":"{:error, :not_in_allowlist}"},{"id":"spn-88572","text":" (deny-by-default)"}]}],"id":"blk-59243","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-59246","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-88573","text":"Otherwise → "},{"id":"spn-88574","marks":["code"],"text":":ok"}]}],"id":"blk-59245","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":true},{"id":"blk-59247","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-88575","text":"Wiring Delegatic into OS-011 replay"}]},{"id":"blk-59248","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-88576","text":"The OS-011 spec §4.4 requires that every destructive replay edge obtain a "},{"id":"spn-88577","marks":["italic"],"text":"fresh"},{"id":"spn-88578","text":" authorization — prior authorization does not carry. Delegatic's "},{"id":"spn-88579","marks":["code"],"text":"authorizer_for/1"},{"id":"spn-88580","text":" returns a function that re-issues a new block on every call, producing exactly the semantics OS-011 demands:"}]},{"id":"blk-59249","kind":"code","language":"elixir","text":"# Recorded trace: destructive edges carry OLD authorization blocks\n# Replay stripper: body-os.Replay strips them before dispatch\n# Delegatic authorizer: fresh block for every edge that makes it through policy\n# Session: enforces the destructive-action gate on the fresh block"},{"id":"blk-59250","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-88581","text":"See "},{"id":"spn-88582","marks":["code"],"text":"body-os/test/delegatic_integration_test.exs"},{"id":"spn-88583","text":" for the end-to-end test that exercises this flow — both the success path (allowlist policy → replay succeeds) and the failure path (readonly policy → replay halts with "},{"id":"spn-88584","marks":["code"],"text":"reason: \"authorization_failure\""},{"id":"spn-88585","text":")."}]},{"id":"blk-59251","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-88586","text":"Running the suite"}]},{"id":"blk-59252","kind":"code","language":"text","text":"mix deps.get\nmix test"},{"id":"blk-59253","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-88587","text":"References"}]},{"id":"blk-59254","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-59256","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-88588","marks":["code"],"text":"delegatic.com/docs/spec/README.md"},{"id":"spn-88589","text":" — full v0.2 spec (organizations, memberships, effective policy, dashboard)"}]}],"id":"blk-59255","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-59258","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-88590","marks":["code"],"text":"opensentience.org/docs/spec/OS-011-EMBODIMENT.md"},{"id":"spn-88591","text":" §4.4 — AuthorizationBlock contract"}]}],"id":"blk-59257","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-59260","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-88592","marks":["code"],"text":"body-os/"},{"id":"spn-88593","text":" + "},{"id":"spn-88594","marks":["code"],"text":"body-browser/"},{"id":"spn-88595","text":" — OS-011 providers whose Replay flows consume Delegatic authorizers"}]}],"id":"blk-59259","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":false},{"id":"blk-59261","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-88596","text":"License"}]},{"id":"blk-59262","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-88597","text":"Apache-2.0"}]}],"edges":[],"id":"bagaaierampipkeabdyk7x3oftbibhpg2ipkzc6hfxqyxkalnyfeiekmnbnda","vocabulary":"ampersand.docs.fs.v1"}